\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Three contrasting network morphology contexts, drawn from archived projected road and facility geometry. Blue indicates the primary ground route and dashed blue the detour; orange denotes low-altitude connections. Thin blue-grey routes show auxiliary ground ODs, and muted orange dashed lines show background air connections where present. D1/H1 mark reference endpoints, V3 a backup landing site, and D2/H2/C2/C3 auxiliary facilities. Co-located landing nodes are not labeled separately. Closure marks the reference disrupted road link. Auxiliary routes describe site context, not additional E1 missions. Maps use a common projected scale and 500 m scale bars. Road and water data: \textcopyright {} OpenStreetMap contributors. Facilities, air operations and disturbances are modeled.}}{12}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig02}{{2}{12}{Three contrasting network morphology contexts, drawn from archived projected road and facility geometry. Blue indicates the primary ground route and dashed blue the detour; orange denotes low-altitude connections. Thin blue-grey routes show auxiliary ground ODs, and muted orange dashed lines show background air connections where present. D1/H1 mark reference endpoints, V3 a backup landing site, and D2/H2/C2/C3 auxiliary facilities. Co-located landing nodes are not labeled separately. Closure marks the reference disrupted road link. Auxiliary routes describe site context, not additional E1 missions. Maps use a common projected scale and 500 m scale bars. Road and water data: \textcopyright {} OpenStreetMap contributors. Facilities, air operations and disturbances are modeled}{figure.2}{}}
