\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Supervisory decision regimes from E1 first-decision logs. (a) Site A candidate geometry relates the air ETA advantage to the best remaining deadline margin; symbols distinguish preemption. Repeated locations represent multiple matched states. (b) Air selections when faster air requires preemption and ground remains timely, with 20, 60 and 20 states at A, B and C. (c) Among states with no candidate predicted timely, observed late counts are 40/40 at A and 24/27 at C per policy; B has no such states. First candidate snapshots match across B1, B2 and B4b in all 720 scenario--seed states. Subsequent actions and trajectories may differ. ETA-based groups are descriptive, not a new policy score.}}{18}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig04}{{4}{18}{Supervisory decision regimes from E1 first-decision logs. (a) Site A candidate geometry relates the air ETA advantage to the best remaining deadline margin; symbols distinguish preemption. Repeated locations represent multiple matched states. (b) Air selections when faster air requires preemption and ground remains timely, with 20, 60 and 20 states at A, B and C. (c) Among states with no candidate predicted timely, observed late counts are 40/40 at A and 24/27 at C per policy; B has no such states. First candidate snapshots match across B1, B2 and B4b in all 720 scenario--seed states. Subsequent actions and trajectories may differ. ETA-based groups are descriptive, not a new policy score}{figure.4}{}}
